  "id": "Compound::DB00493 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Cefotaxime, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is shown to bind to Slc22a11 and Slc22a8, both of which are involved in the transport of organic anions across cellular membranes. These transporters are further linked to Slc22a6, suggesting a potential role for Cefotaxime in modulating the activity of Slc22a6. The evidence from the three paths collectively indicates that Cefotaxime may influence Slc22a6 through the regulation of organic anion transport, possibly by interfering with the function of Slc22a11 or Slc22a8. The final scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The observed interactions highlight the importance of Slc22a6 in organic anion transport and suggest that Cefotaxime could act as a modulator of this process, potentially with implications for drug metabolism and transport.",
